     [0;90;1m│[0m [0;96mNote: A primitive a constructor holds is named by a record field, by a type of its own, or by nothing at all, and the last leaves a reader counting arguments to find out which one it is. A constructor of one field needs none of that, because its name is that field's name. A constructor of several names the whole of what it holds and no part of it, so a primitive among them is named nowhere and two fields a caller has the wrong way round still typecheck. Give each of them a newtype, which is what the guide asks for, or write the constructor with record syntax, which names them without asking for a type. Bool is HsNoDomainBool's business, and the fields of a record constructor are named already.[0m
